    "holeAtoH": "Holes A to H: the fundamental deviation is the lower deviation EI (positive or zero); ES = EI + IT. ISO 286-1:1988, 9.2 and Figure 18.",
    "holeKtoZC": "Holes K to ZC: the fundamental deviation is the upper deviation ES; EI = ES - IT. ISO 286-1:1988, 9.2 and Figure 18.",
    "holeDelta": "K, M and N in grades up to IT8 (incl.) and P to ZC in grades up to IT7 (incl.): ES = tabulated value + Delta of that grade (fundamentalDeviations.delta). The standard's examples: K7 at 18 to 30 mm, ES = -2 + 8 = +6 um; S6 at 18 to 30 mm, ES = -35 + 4 = -31 um. ISO 286-1:1988, Table 3, footnote 3.",
